<PageLayout
  title="Contact Billwright"
  description="How to get in touch about Billwright — bug reports, missing countries and template requests."
  heading="Contact"
  standfirst="Worth telling us about: a tax line that is wrong for your country, a template you need, or anything that produced a broken PDF."
>
  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>
    If a number looks wrong, check which figure the calculator is asking for — margin and markup in
    particular are easy to swap. The <a href="/guides">guides</a> cover the questions that come up
    most often.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting something broken</h2>
  <p>
    The useful details are: which page, which browser, what you typed and what you expected instead.
    If a PDF came out wrong, the template name and the number of line items usually pin it down.
  </p>

  <h2>Asking for a country or a template</h2>
  <p>
    Adding a country means adding its tax name, standard rate, currency and number format, so tell us
    all four if you know them. Template requests are easiest to act on with an example of the layout
    you have been sending.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
